59	/**
60	 * A specialization of {@link FormattingConversionService} configured by default with
61	 * converters and formatters appropriate for most Spring Boot applications.
62	 * <p>
63	 * Designed for direct instantiation but also exposes the static
64	 * {@link #addApplicationConverters} and
65	 * {@link #addApplicationFormatters(FormatterRegistry)} utility methods for ad-hoc use
66	 * against registry instance.
67	 *
68	 * @author Phillip Webb
69	 * @author Shixiong Guo
70	 * @since 2.0.0
71	 */
